  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Site Coordination, Management Services, and Monitoring of Displacement and Multisectoral Humanitarian Needs in Communities and Sites Affected by Displacement/Return in Eastern DRC, Democratic Republic of the Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) is facing one of the largest and most complex humanitarian crises in the world. The crisis affects a large part of its population and is the result of many factors &#x2013;including the activism of armed groups and subsequent armed conflict, inter-community conflicts, disease, and natural disasters. The constant threat of violence and insecurity, particularly in the eastern provinces has led to a massive increase in population displacement in the past year. The situation shows no signs of easing and will likely be exacerbated in the coming months with the upcoming elections. 
 
Through this project, IOM is improving the well-being of IDPs and host populations by reinforcing the coordination and management of sites and capturing critical information on population mobility and regularly process and disseminate information to provide a better understanding of the movements and evolving needs of displaced populations. IOM is strengthening its Camp Coordination Camp Management (CCCM) response at cluster level, after the recent activation of the CCCM Cluster, as well as enhancing data consolidation and harmonization on population movements through a comprehensive and unified approach to data collection, sharing, and use.</narrative>
  </description>
